WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.142
Giving and Receiving Feedback.

2
00:00:02.422 --> 00:00:06.667
Day 18 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Communication phase.

3
00:00:08.417 --> 00:00:09.441
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.721 --> 00:00:18.127
Today's goal: give feedback that is specific, kind and useful, and receive feedback (even unfair feedback) without becoming defensive.

5
00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:20.330
Part 1.

6
00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:21.933
Why feedback is hard.

7
00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:25.871
We worry about hurting people or being disliked.

8
00:00:26.151 --> 00:00:30.737
We give vague feedback (good job, needs improvement) that nobody can act on.

9
00:00:31.017 --> 00:00:34.281
When we receive it, we hear criticism of us, not of our work.

10
00:00:35.631 --> 00:00:36.506
Part 2.

11
00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:39.047
Giving feedback: the SBI model.

12
00:00:40.297 --> 00:00:41.663
Here is a quick table:

13
00:00:41.943 --> 00:00:43.201
Part, and Example.

14
00:00:43.481 --> 00:00:44.505
Situation:

15
00:00:44.785 --> 00:00:46.449
In yesterday's client demo...

16
00:00:46.729 --> 00:00:54.025
Behaviour (what you saw or heard, not your opinion of them): ...you explained the new search feature using the client's own data...

17
00:00:54.305 --> 00:00:57.591
Impact: ...and the client said it was the clearest demo they've had.

18
00:00:57.871 --> 00:00:58.617
Next:

19
00:00:58.897 --> 00:01:00.924
Could you show the team how you prepared it?

20
00:01:02.274 --> 00:01:04.471
Positive feedback (do it more often).

21
00:01:04.751 --> 00:01:08.591
The way you handled the angry customer on the call was really calm.

22
00:01:08.871 --> 00:01:10.343
It stopped the escalation.

23
00:01:10.623 --> 00:01:12.223
Thanks for writing the runbook.

24
00:01:12.503 --> 00:01:15.319
It saved me an hour during last night's incident.

25
00:01:16.669 --> 00:01:19.720
Improvement feedback (private, timely, specific).

26
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:20.939
You could say:

27
00:01:21.219 --> 00:01:24.077
Can I share some feedback about this morning's stand-up?

28
00:01:24.357 --> 00:01:30.501
When you went into the database details for ten minutes, the meeting ran over and two people missed their next call.

29
00:01:30.781 --> 00:01:35.432
Next time, could you share the headline in stand-up and take the details offline?

30
00:01:36.782 --> 00:01:38.147
Here is a quick table:

31
00:01:38.427 --> 00:01:41.542
Vague or personal, and Specific and about behaviour.

32
00:01:41.822 --> 00:01:42.803
You're careless.:

33
00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:45.558
Two PRs this week were merged without tests.

34
00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:46.841
Great job!:

35
00:01:47.121 --> 00:01:50.086
Your test for the empty-cart case caught a real bug.

36
00:01:50.366 --> 00:01:52.137
You need to communicate better.:

37
00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:54.998
I didn't know the release was blocked until Friday.

38
00:01:55.278 --> 00:01:57.155
A message on Tuesday would have helped.

39
00:01:57.435 --> 00:01:58.779
You always interrupt.:

40
00:01:59.059 --> 00:02:03.091
In the last two meetings, you finished Priya's sentences before she was done.

41
00:02:04.441 --> 00:02:05.337
Part 3.

42
00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:06.855
Receiving feedback.

43
00:02:08.105 --> 00:02:09.022
Step 1:

44
00:02:09.302 --> 00:02:11.841
Pause: breathe; don't reply immediately.

45
00:02:12.121 --> 00:02:13.038
Step 2:

46
00:02:13.318 --> 00:02:14.001
Thank:

47
00:02:14.281 --> 00:02:15.518
Thanks for telling me.

48
00:02:15.798 --> 00:02:16.715
Step 3:

49
00:02:16.995 --> 00:02:17.934
Clarify:

50
00:02:18.214 --> 00:02:19.707
Can you give me an example?

51
00:02:19.987 --> 00:02:20.947
Step 4:

52
00:02:21.227 --> 00:02:23.169
Reflect: take a day if you need to.

53
00:02:23.449 --> 00:02:24.409
Step 5:

54
00:02:24.689 --> 00:02:25.883
Act and follow up:

55
00:02:26.163 --> 00:02:28.915
I tried your suggestion; did you notice a difference?

56
00:02:30.265 --> 00:02:31.631
Here is a quick table:

57
00:02:31.911 --> 00:02:33.020
Instead of, and Say.

58
00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.303
Yes, but...:

59
00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:35.991
I hadn't seen it that way.

60
00:02:36.271 --> 00:02:37.145
Tell me more.

61
00:02:37.425 --> 00:02:38.535
That's not true!:

62
00:02:38.815 --> 00:02:40.756
Can you help me understand what you saw?

63
00:02:41.036 --> 00:02:42.295
Everyone does that.:

64
00:02:42.575 --> 00:02:43.321
Thanks.

65
00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:44.689
I'll work on it.

66
00:02:44.969 --> 00:02:46.164
Silence and hurt:

67
00:02:46.444 --> 00:02:49.303
I'd like to think about this and come back to you tomorrow.

68
00:02:50.653 --> 00:02:51.570
Part 4.

69
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.173
Asking for feedback.

70
00:02:54.423 --> 00:02:57.281
What's one thing I could do differently in design reviews?

71
00:02:57.561 --> 00:03:00.825
On a scale of 1 to 10, how clear was my presentation?

72
00:03:01.105 --> 00:03:02.407
What would make it a 10?

73
00:03:02.687 --> 00:03:05.396
What should I keep doing, and what should I stop doing?

74
00:03:06.746 --> 00:03:07.706
Part 5.

75
00:03:07.986 --> 00:03:10.717
Conversation 1: giving feedback to a peer.

76
00:03:11.967 --> 00:03:13.993
Here is how the conversation goes.

77
00:03:14.273 --> 00:03:16.577
Hi Arun, do you have five minutes?

78
00:03:16.857 --> 00:03:20.249
I'd like to share some feedback about the PR reviews.

79
00:03:20.529 --> 00:03:21.233
Sure.

80
00:03:21.513 --> 00:03:22.729
Is something wrong?

81
00:03:23.009 --> 00:03:25.185
Not wrong, just something I've noticed.

82
00:03:25.465 --> 00:03:31.375
On my last three PRs, the comments said things like this is bad without explaining why.

83
00:03:31.655 --> 00:03:32.337
Oh.

84
00:03:32.617 --> 00:03:34.217
I was in a hurry, I guess.

85
00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:37.167
The conversation continues.

86
00:03:37.447 --> 00:03:38.813
I understand.

87
00:03:39.093 --> 00:03:42.229
The impact is that I spend time guessing what you mean.

88
00:03:42.509 --> 00:03:45.581
Could you add a short reason, or a suggestion?

89
00:03:45.861 --> 00:03:47.098
That's fair.

90
00:03:47.378 --> 00:03:48.423
I'll do that.

91
00:03:48.703 --> 00:03:49.834
Anything else?

92
00:03:50.114 --> 00:03:53.463
No, and to be clear, your reviews catch real bugs.

93
00:03:53.743 --> 00:03:55.279
That's really valuable.

94
00:03:55.559 --> 00:03:57.330
Thanks for telling me directly.

95
00:03:58.680 --> 00:03:59.619
Part 6.

96
00:03:59.899 --> 00:04:02.523
Conversation 2: receiving tough feedback.

97
00:04:03.773 --> 00:04:05.799
Here is how the conversation goes.

98
00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:09.173
I want to share some feedback about the client call yesterday.

99
00:04:09.453 --> 00:04:11.031
Sure, please go ahead.

100
00:04:11.311 --> 00:04:16.346
When the client asked about the delay, you said it's not our fault, the bank changed the API.

101
00:04:16.626 --> 00:04:18.162
It sounded defensive.

102
00:04:18.442 --> 00:04:19.914
Thanks for telling me.

103
00:04:20.194 --> 00:04:22.263
Can I ask what you would have said?

104
00:04:23.613 --> 00:04:25.213
The conversation continues.

105
00:04:25.493 --> 00:04:30.656
Acknowledge their concern first, then explain the cause briefly, and focus on the new plan.

106
00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:32.109
That makes sense.

107
00:04:32.389 --> 00:04:34.352
I'll try that in the next call.

108
00:04:34.632 --> 00:04:35.571
Great.

109
00:04:35.851 --> 00:04:38.155
I know the bank really did cause it, by the way.

110
00:04:38.435 --> 00:04:40.013
I appreciate that.

111
00:04:40.293 --> 00:04:43.152
Could you give me feedback after the next call too?

112
00:04:43.432 --> 00:04:44.563
Absolutely.

113
00:04:45.913 --> 00:04:46.851
Part 7.

114
00:04:47.131 --> 00:04:48.177
Speak today.

115
00:04:49.427 --> 00:04:53.181
Give one piece of specific positive feedback using SBI.

116
00:04:53.461 --> 00:04:54.677
Ask one person:

117
00:04:54.957 --> 00:04:57.731
What's one thing I could do better? and just say Thank you.

118
00:04:59.081 --> 00:05:00.617
That's the end of this lesson.

119
00:05:00.897 --> 00:05:05.569
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

120
00:05:05.849 --> 00:05:11.950
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

